// 3.1 LINKAGE probe -- IR-ONLY, deliberately never built or run.
//
// A single @export puts the whole translation unit into C-LIBRARY mode: the runtime-init entry is
// emitted under a non-`main` symbol so a C host can supply its own main. That is correct behaviour,
// and it is also why this cannot live in _f31_unbox_elim_probe.nova -- that probe must RUN, and a
// library has no main to run. So the export case gets its own file and the gate only emits IR for
// it.
//
// WHAT IS BEING GUARDED. Ordinary functions are now emitted `internal` so LLVM can inline them
// (with the unbox removal, that is the whole 1.69x -> 1.00x win). @export is the one case where the
// symbol IS the interface. Internalising it still COMPILES and still LINKS as a library -- a C host
// simply cannot resolve the function, and nothing in this repo would notice. That is precisely the
// kind of silent, far-away breakage worth a structural assertion.

@export
fn nova_exported_add(a: int, b: int) -> int
    a + b

@export
fn nova_exported_scale(v: float) -> float
    v * 2.0

// Not exported: must be internal even in library mode, and must keep working as a callee.
fn helper_add(a: int, b: int) -> int
    a + b

fn main()
    print(str(nova_exported_add(1, 2)) + " " + str(helper_add(3, 4)) + " " + str(nova_exported_scale(1.5)))
